========================================================================
  PART 2: EXACT Var(H) — CAN WE DERIVE IT?
========================================================================


  Var(H) = E[H²] - E[H]².

  We know E[H] = n!/2^{n-1} (each permutation is a HP with probability 1/2^{n-1}).

  For E[H²], we need the second moment. H² = (Σ_σ Π_arcs)² = Σ_{σ,τ} Π_{arcs of σ ∩ τ}.

  Two Hamiltonian paths σ and τ share some arcs. If they share k arcs:
    E[Π_{arcs of σ} × Π_{arcs of τ}] = 1/2^{2(n-1)-k}
  because 2(n-1)-k DISTINCT arc choices are made.

  So: E[H²] = Σ_{σ,τ} 1/2^{2(n-1)-overlap(σ,τ)}
            = Σ_{k=0}^{n-1} N(k) / 2^{2(n-1)-k}

  where N(k) = #{pairs (σ,τ) with exactly k common arcs}.

  This is a COMBINATORIAL quantity depending on the overlap structure
  of Hamiltonian paths in K_n.

  n = 3:
    N(k) overlap distribution:
      k=0: N(k) = 18 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=1: N(k) = 12 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=2: N(k) = 6 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
    E[H] = 1.5
    E[H²] from overlap = 4.125
    Var(H) = 1.875
    Var(H) exact (from S104) = 0.75

  n = 4:
    N(k) overlap distribution:
      k=0: N(k) = 264 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=1: N(k) = 216 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=2: N(k) = 72 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=3: N(k) = 24 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
    E[H] = 3.0
    E[H²] from overlap = 18.375
    Var(H) = 9.375
    Var(H) exact (from S104) = not available

  n = 5:
    N(k) overlap distribution:
      k=0: N(k) = 6360 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=1: N(k) = 5280 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=2: N(k) = 2160 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=3: N(k) = 480 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
      k=4: N(k) = 120 (fraction of all (σ,τ) pairs with k shared arcs)
    E[H] = 7.5
